name 'self-paced-TCaAI-L1-PBLCFY'
title 'Check for Understanding'
description ''
question 'A teacher is planning to teach Thinking Critically About AI and asks: “What makes this unit truly project-based rather than just a collection of engaging AI lessons?” Which explanation best reflects the design of the unit?'
wrong 'Students explore AI tools through interactive activities and complete a final project to demonstrate what they learned.'
right 'Students move through themed milestones where each investigation contributes evidence that shapes and revises a public-facing Responsible AI Use Guide.'
wrong 'Students collaborate during lessons, discuss ethical issues, and present their opinions about AI at the end of the unit.'
wrong 'Students learn key AI concepts first and then apply them in a creative project designed to showcase their understanding.'


markdown <<MARKDOWN

MARKDOWN

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
#### **Explanation:** Option B is correct because it captures the core structure of Project-Based Learning as implemented in this unit: students do not complete investigations and then move on to a separate project at the end. Instead, each milestone investigation generates evidence that directly shapes and refines a section of the Responsible AI Use Guide. Learning unfolds iteratively, with students revisiting ideas, incorporating feedback, and strengthening their claims over time.
MARKDOWN

allow_multiple_attempts true